{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774045331,"nonce":"Ru/xIyDDvzL71f+y+NVFumG3A40=","title":"P1: MCP channel server — stdio MCP server over Mandible HTTP API","message":"Parent: 73e0adf\n\nNew channel-server/ directory with MCP server implementation.\n\n## Files\n- channel-server/index.ts — entry point, stdio transport, MCP server\n- channel-server/tools.ts — 5 tool handlers (check_inbox, report_status, submit_auth, get_issues, request_work)\n- channel-server/notifications.ts — SSE listener pushing Mandible events as MCP channel notifications\n- channel-server/client.ts — HTTP client for Mandible API (localhost:19420)\n- channel-server/types.ts — shared types\n- package.json/tsconfig.json — build integration\n\n## Design\n- Uses @modelcontextprotocol/sdk (already a dependency)\n- stdio transport (Claude Code spawns as subprocess)\n- Stateless: all state in daemon, accessed via HTTP\n- instructions field teaches Claude about Mandible events\n- Connects to /api/events SSE for real-time event → MCP notification push\n- Tools return structured JSON that Claude can act on","files":null}]}